WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.220
How do we find all the factors of 24?

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.820
It's simple!

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.800
We write the number as a product of two positive numbers.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.580
We have to think of all possible combinations though.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.860
How do we write it as a product of two numbers?

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.120
Let me give you an example.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.580
It can be written as 1 multiplied by 24.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.560
We have written 24 as a product of two numbers.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.760
But remember, we have to think of all possible combinations.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.140
It can also be written as 2 times 12.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:40.080
Wait, it can also be written as 3 times 8.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.560
Are there any more combinations?

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.160
Yes, it can be written as 4 times 6.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.440
That's it. There is no other product of two positive numbers

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.640
that would result in 24.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.920
Wait!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.520
How do we know that all products have been covered?

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.800
Okay, so always use this logic when you are writing a number

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.120
as a product of two numbers.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.900
Start off with one.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.240
Every number is obviously divisible by 1! Write that product first.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.500
Then see if the number is divisible by 2, which is the next natural number.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:17.560
If yes,

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.480
we write the product as we have written it here.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.780
Then we move on to the next natural number 3.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.560
Is 24 divisible by 3?

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.400
Yes, so we write the product here.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:30.940
Then four,

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.960
24 is divisible by 4 and we wrote that product here.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.620
And after 4 we have 5.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.120
Is 24 divisible by 5?

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:45.560
No it isn't! So we cannot write it as a product of 5 and another number.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.000
And the next number is 6.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.160
But 6 onwards is already covered here.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.600
That's when we know that we have covered

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.320
all possible products of two numbers.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.400
The numbers covered are in a "U" shape.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.160
Anyway, that's all we had to do.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.800
What are the factors of 24 then?

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.120
All these numbers individually are the factors of 24.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:19.420
We can say that the factors of 24 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12 and 24.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.780
We write the number as all possible products of two numbers

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.980
and then each of the numbers become a factor of that number.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.260
Let's try finding the factors of another number.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.480
We need to find all the factors of 30.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.920
To do that, all we have to do is write 30

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.060
as all possible products of two numbers.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.840
I will be telling you the answer in some time.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:48.160
Meanwhile, you can try writing down the combinations in your notebook.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.600
We can start off with the number 1.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.940
30 can be written as 1 multiplied by 30.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:02.400
This is the simplest and the most obvious combination.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.780
One is always a factor of all numbers.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.820
Then we move on to 2.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.080
Is 30 divisible by 2?

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.860
Yes and the product can be written as 2 multiplied by 15.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.460
Is 30 divisible by 3?

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.880
Yes, the product can be written as 3 multiplied by 10.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.060
Is 30 divisible by 4?

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.300
No it isn't, so we cannot

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.440
write a product with 4 as one of the numbers.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:34.140
What about 5? Yes, 30 is divisible by 5.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.340
And the product can be written as 5 multiplied by 6.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.060
Next number is 6 which is already covered here.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.000
And the numbers after 6 are covered here.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.320
That's when we know that we have exhausted all possibilities.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.480
These are the only four ways in which we can write 30

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.000
as a product of two numbers.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.920
So we can say that these eight numbers

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.760
individually are the factors of 30.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:09.120
The factors are 1, 2, 3 ,5, 6 ,10, 15 and 30.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.380
How can we define factors then?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.880
Well, the factors of a number

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.440
are basically exact divisors of that number.

